## 5. Sample SQL JOIN queries

### Join projects with their images
```sql
SELECT
  p.id,
  p.title,
  p.slug,
  pi.id AS image_id,
  pi.url,
  pi."order"
FROM "Project" p
LEFT JOIN "ProjectImage" pi
  ON pi."projectId" = p.id
WHERE p."deletedAt" IS NULL
ORDER BY p.createdAt DESC, pi."order";
```

### Join activity logs with users
```sql
SELECT
  al.id,
  al.action,
  al.details,
  u.email,
  u.name
FROM "ActivityLog" al
LEFT JOIN "User" u
  ON u.email = al."userEmail"
ORDER BY al."createdAt" DESC;
```

## 6. Data flow between tables
- Users authenticate through `User` and perform admin actions.
- Admin actions are recorded in `ActivityLog` for audit purposes.
- Content sections such as `HeroSection`, `AboutSection`, `Service`, `FAQ`, `Testimonial`, and `TeamMember` are used to build the public website pages.
- `Project` stores portfolio case-study data and `ProjectImage` stores the related visual assets for each project.
- `ContactMessage` captures inbound inquiries; `ContactDetails` provides display/contact information.
- `NewsletterSubscriber` stores visitor subscriptions.
- `SEOSettings` and `SystemSettings` configure metadata, branding, and site-wide behavior.

