## 11. Best practices before UPDATE or DELETE
- Always run a `SELECT` first to confirm the target rows.
- Prefer `UPDATE ... SET deletedAt = NOW()` over `DELETE` for most content tables because the schema uses soft delete.
- Wrap changes in a transaction when modifying multiple tables.
- Use a precise `WHERE` clause based on `id`, `slug`, or another unique field.
- Backup the database before bulk changes.
- Test in a non-production environment first.
- Review cascading effects before deleting a parent row such as a project, because its images will be removed automatically.

